From 7072c8466ae576060369618cb5615bacac1283e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:11:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] drm/panfrost: Freeze the reset workqueue during system
 sleep

pm_runtime_force_suspend() ignores the usage count, and from
drm_sched_stop() on the GPU looks idle, so system sleep can power it off
under a running timeout handler or reset work. Make their workqueue
freezable: the freezer waits for them before devices are suspended.

Fixes: f3ba91228e8e ("drm/panfrost: Add initial panfrost driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/sashiko-outbox-210830@kernel.org/
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20261113-panfrost-long-jobs-v3-0-80ae78d38f6e@gmail.com?part=13
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
index d59b486..a3c90c5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
@@ -889,7 +889,7 @@ int panfrost_jm_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	pfdev->reset.wq = alloc_ordered_workqueue("panfrost-reset", 0);
+	pfdev->reset.wq = alloc_ordered_workqueue("panfrost-reset", WQ_FREEZABLE);
 	if (!pfdev->reset.wq)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	args.timeout_wq = pfdev->reset.wq;
-- 
